d}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 & 4 & 3 \\\\ 5 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & -3 \\\\ -5 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(2,-5),(-4,3),(-3,-2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283657 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283658 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283659 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283660 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283661 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1041 "selection" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283659 13194139534335 true] [17592186283656 1110 #uuid "7d09efa5-6632-5143-9936-dbe1529132a3" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283657 1034 "I and III only" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283657 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534335 true] [17592186283657 1111 #uuid "16a8b80c-163f-5ec7-a556-41c89abe1d1c" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283658 1034 "I only" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283658 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534335 true] [17592186283658 1111 #uuid "73c598f7-e612-5419-ba17-12badeb6efb0" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283659 1034 "III only" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283659 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534335 true] [17592186283659 1111 #uuid "74e3752b-b1ce-52c2-8939-f0e1ccbee377" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283660 1034 "I and II only" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283660 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534335 true] [17592186283660 1111 #uuid "15703ce6-3c1e-54f1-9d0d-1031b93539c9" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283661 1034 "II only" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283661 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534335 true] [17592186283661 1111 #uuid "4f55e929-5a76-5c6c-b696-95eeba30b65b" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283662 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283663 13194139534335 true] [17592186283662 1089 "q-160371" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283662 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534335 true] [17592186283662 1100 "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(6,-1),(-4,1),(3,5).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ about the origin?\n\n- $(-6,-1)$\n- $(4,-1)$\n- $(3,-5)$" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283662 1113 #uuid "f0af2085-c5e5-5d4f-bf4d-73318bbad63b" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283662 1145 "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by an angle of ${180}^{∘}$ is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{{180}^{∘}},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{{180}^{∘}}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}6 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(-6,1),(4,-1),(-3,-5).$ \n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283664 13194139534335 true] [17592186283663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283665 13194139534335 true] [17592186283663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283666 13194139534335 true] [17592186283663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283667 13194139534335 true] [17592186283663 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283668 13194139534335 true] [17592186283663 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534335 true] [17592186283663 1041 "selection" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283663 1104 #edb/ref 17592186283668 131941395