[17592186283739 1017 #edb/ref 17592186283740 13194139534335 true] [17592186283739 1089 "q-8394" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283739 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534335 true] [17592186283739 1100 "A triangle $S$ has vertices at $(0,0),(1,5),(2,3).$ Which of the following are coordinates of the vertices of ${S}^{′},$ the image of $S$ under the counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians about the origin?\n\n- $(-5,1)$\n- $(0,-2)$\n- $(2,-3)$" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283739 1113 #uuid "5e62f917-e247-5e01-9129-0fa18b8a8257" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283739 1145 "The counterclockwise rotation ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by an angle of $\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ radians is given by the matrix\n\n$$\nR=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $S$ under the action of ${R}_{\\pi /2},$ we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of $S:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}X & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under ${R}_{\\pi /2}$ by calculating the matrix product $RX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}RX & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the respective vertices of ${S}^{′}$ are $(0,0),(-5,1),(-3,2).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283741 13194139534335 true] [17592186283740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283742 13194139534335 true] [17592186283740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283743 13194139534335 true] [17592186283740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283744 13194139534335 true] [17592186283740 1000 #edb/ref 17592186283745 13194139534335 true] [17592186283740 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534335 true] [17592186283740 1041 "selection" 13194139534335 true] [17592186283740 1104 #edb/ref 175921